{"tool_name":"expansionhunter_denovo","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ExpansionHunter_Denovo","home":"https://github.com/Illumina/ExpansionHunterDenovo","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"A computational method for locating known and novel repeat expansions in short-read sequencing data.\n\nA suite of tools for detecting expansions of short tandem repeats.\n\nExpansionHunter Denovo (EHdn) is a suite of tools for detecting novel expansions of short tandem repeats (STRs). EHdn is intended for analysis of a collection of BAM/CRAM files containing alignments of short (100-200bp) reads.","addition_date":"2020-01-14T19:42:02Z","last_update_date":"2020-12-28T15:16:11Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Suite"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:ExpansionHunter_Denovo","documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/Illumina/ExpansionHunterDenovo/blob/master/documentation/00_Introduction.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Read mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3198"},{"term":"Repeat sequence detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0379"}]}],"name":"ExpansionHunter Denovo","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/863035"},{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-020-02017-z","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020 The Author(s).Repeat expansions are responsible for over 40 monogenic disorders, and undoubtedly more pathogenic repeat expansions remain to be discovered. Existing methods for detecting repeat expansions in short-read sequencing data require predefined repeat catalogs. Recent discoveries emphasize the need for methods that do not require pre-specified candidate repeats. To address this need, we introduce ExpansionHunter Denovo, an efficient catalog-free method for genome-wide repeat expansion detection. Analysis of real and simulated data shows that our method can identify large expansions of 41 out of 44 pathogenic repeats, including nine recently reported non-reference repeat expansions not discoverable via existing methods.","authors":[{"name":"Bahlo M."},{"name":"Bennett M.F."},{"name":"Bentley D.R."},{"name":"Chen S."},{"name":"Dolzhenko E."},{"name":"Eberle M.A."},{"name":"Gainullin V.G."},{"name":"Gross A.M."},{"name":"Lajoie B.R."},{"name":"Narzisi G."},{"name":"Nguyen C."},{"name":"Richmond P.A."},{"name":"Scherer S.W."},{"name":"Taft R.J."},{"name":"Trost B."},{"name":"Van Vugt J.J.F.A."},{"name":"Veldink J.H."},{"name":"Wasserman W.W."},{"name":"Yuen R.K.C."}],"citationCount":10,"date":"2020-04-28T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"ExpansionHunter Denovo: A computational method for locating known and novel repeat expansions in short-read sequencing data"},"pmcid":"PMC7187524","pmid":"32345345"}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA polymorphism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2885"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"},{"term":"Sequence composition, complexity and repeats","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0157"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"ExpansionHunter Denovo","home":"https://bio.tools/ExpansionHunter_Denovo","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"A computational method for locating known and novel repeat expansions in short-read sequencing data.\n\nA suite of tools for detecting expansions of short tandem repeats.\n\nExpansionHunter Denovo (EHdn) is a suite of tools for detecting novel expansions of short tandem repeats (STRs). EHdn is intended for analysis of a collection of BAM/CRAM files containing alignments of short (100-200bp) reads.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:expansionhunter_denovo/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binar